In contrast to all helical ribbons detailed so far, we show one framework that is based on helices containing both triangles and quadrangles. A framework, \(\mathrm{Co}(\mathrm{BDC})\) contains SBUs of general formula \([\mathrm{M}(-\mathrm{COO})_{2}]_{\infty},\) being composed of triangles and quadrangles in a ratio of 2:1 (Figure 71).238 The \(\mathrm{Co}^{\bar{2}+}\) centers are octahedrally coordinated by four carboxylate \(\mathrm{o}\) and two \(\mu_{2}\) -oxygen from e-urea. The e-urea is not shown in our illustration. The authors have originally described the topology as a trinodal net by considering BDC as \(4{\mathrm{-}}c\) and Co as 6-c nodes, forming a \(4_{1}\) helix. However, we assign the carboxylate C as points of extension and therefore obtain a \((4,5)\) -c zbz net with transitivity 2 6 and symmetry \(P4_{1}22\) .

